From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 09:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] gstreamer: stop the pipeline at end-of-media

At natural end-of-stream QGstreamerMediaPlayer tells the application that
playback has stopped:

    mediaStatusChanged(QMediaPlayer::EndOfMedia);
    stateChanged(QMediaPlayer::StoppedState);

but nothing takes the underlying GstPlay pipeline out of GST_STATE_PLAYING.
QGstreamerMediaPlayer::stop() issues gst_play_stop() for exactly that purpose;
the EOS path never does. GstPlay's own EOS handling only updates its reported
GstPlayState, it does not touch the playbin state either.

The result is that a finished player keeps its audio sink open. With the
PulseAudio sink that matters: pulsesink corks its stream only on a
PLAYING->PAUSED transition, so the stream stays uncorked indefinitely even
though QMediaPlayer::playbackState() reports StoppedState. PulseAudio's
module-suspend-on-idle only suspends a sink that has no uncorked inputs, so the
output sink can never be suspended and keeps rendering silence for as long as
the player object lives.

Measured on LuneOS (Qt 6.12.0, GStreamer 1.28.2, Pixel 3a): a QML MediaPlayer
that plays one short boot chime and is then left alone held an uncorked
PulseAudio stream for the entire lifetime of the compositor process. The audio
sink stayed RUNNING and pulseaudio sat at 10.1% of a CPU core permanently;
force-suspending the sink dropped it to 0.1%. On an untouched device the
sink-input was still reported "Corked: no" 35 minutes after the clip had
finished. Adding an explicit stop() from QML at EndOfMedia released it, which
is what identified this path.

Calling gst_play_stop() here makes the pipeline match the state that was just
reported. Replay after EOS is unaffected: play() already resets position and
media status when mediaStatus() == EndOfMedia and then calls gst_play_play(),
which re-prepares a stopped GstPlay.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 .../multimedia/gstreamer/common/qgstreamermediaplayer.cpp    | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

--- a/src/plugins/multimedia/gstreamer/common/qgstreamermediaplayer.cpp
+++ b/src/plugins/multimedia/gstreamer/common/qgstreamermediaplayer.cpp
@@ -675,6 +675,16 @@
             mediaStatusChanged(QMediaPlayer::EndOfMedia);
             stateChanged(QMediaPlayer::StoppedState);
             gstVideoOutput->setActive(false);
+
+            // We have just reported StoppedState, but neither GstPlay's EOS
+            // handling nor anything above takes the pipeline out of
+            // GST_STATE_PLAYING, so the audio sink stays open. With pulsesink
+            // the stream is then never corked - it corks only on a
+            // PLAYING->PAUSED transition - and module-suspend-on-idle can never
+            // suspend the output sink, which keeps rendering silence for as
+            // long as this player lives. Put the pipeline where the state we
+            // just reported says it is.
+            gst_play_stop(m_gstPlay.get());
         }
 
         return false;
